# EnzyRank — git tracks code, data, configs, docs, out-of-fold predictions, small caches and the
# bundled ChemBERTa model. Large, fully-regenerable artifacts stay on disk but are excluded from git
# so the repository remains deployable. Everything excluded here is either downloadable
# (pretrained/README.md) or regenerable (scripts/extract_*.py + reproduce.sh).

# --- Regenerable feature caches (HDF5 embeddings) ---
# Excluded from git: the per-residue caches are multi-GB and the pooled caches exceed GitHub's
# 100 MB file limit. All are regenerable via scripts/extract_*.py. They stay on disk for local use;
# the small .npz caches (substrate fingerprints, ChemBERTa means) ARE tracked.
cache/*.h5
cache/**/*.h5

# Local distribution archive for the complete precomputed cache (shared via Google Drive)
/cache.tar.gz

# --- Large downloaded pretrained encoders (> 1 GB; see pretrained/README.md) ---
pretrained/prot_t5_xl_half_uniref50-enc/
pretrained/esm2_t33_650M_UR50D/
pretrained/ESMC-600M/
# (pretrained/ChemBERTa-77M-MTR/ IS tracked — it is only 14 MB and bundled)

# --- Python / environment noise ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
